  "name": "Turn industry news into LinkedIn posts with AI and auto-post after Gmail approval",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3dd53823-451e-4fc3-84b9-5895368d3372",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## LinkedIn thought leadership from the news, approved from your inbox\nEach weekday morning this workflow takes the newest story from a news feed you choose, writes a LinkedIn post in your voice with your angle, and emails it to you. One click on **Post it** publishes it to LinkedIn; **Skip** discards it. Every story is used once and every post is logged.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Weekdays at 8:00** starts the run; **Your feed and angle** holds the feed URL, your point of view and your email.\n2. **Read the news feed** and **Skip stories already used** (Remove Duplicates across runs) keep only new stories; **Newest first** sorts them by date and **Newest story** takes one.\n3. **Write the LinkedIn post** (PostWire, Write Drafts) drafts it in your voice. Nothing is published yet.\n4. **Ask me to approve it** emails the draft and waits for your click.\n5. **Post to LinkedIn** publishes the exact text you approved and **Published?** logs the link, or logs the error and emails the fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks (one click each: no developer app, no Meta or TikTok review) and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Add a Gmail credential to the three Gmail nodes and a Google Sheets credential; create a sheet with `date, story, source, status, link, note`.\n3. In **Your feed and angle** paste any RSS feed (a Google News search feed works) and write your angle in one or two sentences.\n4. Optional: add Bluesky or Facebook to both PostWire nodes to post the same approved idea there.\n\nFree PostWire plan: 20 posts a month and 2 networks per post, no card; 3 or more networks per post need a paid plan."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
